# CORRECTION appended 2026-08-24 18:35
#
# The probe above labelled www.plugservices.ca and checkin.plugservices.ca as
# "DOES NOT RESOLVE". For www that conclusion is WRONG. The probe ran with
# MaximumRedirection 0, and PowerShell raises an exception on a 3xx that this
# script could not always unpack - so a REDIRECT was recorded as an error.
# www.plugservices.ca demonstrably works: step 9 and step 12 both downloaded
# /site.js from it and matched the sha1 against the deploy manifest.
# Read those two rows as "redirects to the apex", not as "dead".
#
# checkin.plugservices.ca is still believed to have no DNS record - that is a
# known open item - but this probe did not distinguish DNS failure from a
# redirect, so it is NOT proof either.
#
# What this probe DID prove, with 9 paths each and identical byte counts:
#   guest.plugservices.ca     -> forced catch-all, every path returns
#                                portal-guest.html (33,890 bytes)
#   organizer.plugservices.ca -> forced catch-all, every path returns
#                                portal-organizer.html (48,841 bytes)
#   On both, /site.js and /styles.css return text/html. Asset paths ARE
#   swallowed. This is why the portal script tag must be an ABSOLUTE URL.
